---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Chrome Extension - The Whetstone"
  description="Audit any argument while you read. The Whetstone's analytical engine, in your browser's side panel, against the page in view."
  canonicalPath="/extension"
>
  <main class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 pt-10 sm:pt-16 pb-16">

    <nav class="mb-10">
      <a href="/" class="text-xs text-muted hover:text-ink transition-colors">← The Whetstone</a>
    </nav>

    <!-- Hero -->
    <header class="mb-14">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.3em] text-accent uppercase mb-4">Devil's Advocate · Chrome Extension</p>
      <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-5xl text-ink-strong leading-tight mb-5">
        Audit any argument while you read.
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-muted leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        The Whetstone's analytical engine, mounted in Chrome's side panel. Highlight a passage or
        scan the whole article - get the Toulmin structure, the fallacy patterns, the hidden warrants,
        without leaving the page.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Side-panel mockup + pitch -->
    <section class="grid lg:grid-cols-[1fr_360px] gap-10 mb-16 items-start">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-accent mb-4">What it does</h2>
        <p class="text-base text-ink leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Open the side panel on any web page. Run the audit against the article you're reading, or
          select a passage and audit just that. The same eleven-lens engine that powers
          <a href="/" class="text-accent underline">the Reader</a> and
          <a href="/creator/studio" class="text-accent underline">Studio</a> - running
          against the page in front of you.
        </p>
        <p class="text-base text-ink leading-relaxed">
          Built for the moment you're already in: reading an op-ed, a thread, a press release, a
          policy brief. You don't have to copy text into another tab. The argument is there; the
          audit comes to it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Side-panel UI mockup -->
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-hairline shadow-lg bg-surface overflow-hidden">
        <div class="bg-hairline/40 px-3 py-2 border-b border-hairline flex items-center gap-1.5">
          <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-red-400"></span>
          <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-amber-400"></span>
          <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-green-400"></span>
          <span class="ml-2 text-xs text-muted uppercase tracking-wider">Side panel</span>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest text-accent uppercase mb-2">Devil's Advocate</p>
          <p class="font-serif text-sm text-ink-strong mb-3 leading-snug">
            Audit this article?
          </p>
          <button class="w-full bg-accent text-white text-xs font-semibold py-2 rounded-md mb-2 cursor-default">
            Audit whole page
          </button>
          <button class="w-full border border-hairline text-ink text-xs font-semibold py-2 rounded-md mb-4 cursor-default">
            Audit selected text
          </button>

          <div class="border-t border-hairline pt-3 space-y-2">
            <div class="rounded-md bg-red-50 border border-red-200 p-2">
              <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-red-700 mb-0.5">High · 88%</p>
              <p class="text-xs text-ink leading-snug">False dilemma in paragraph 3</p>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-md bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 p-2">
              <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-amber-700 mb-0.5">Medium · 72%</p>
              <p class="text-xs text-ink leading-snug">Unstated warrant: "expert consensus implies policy"</p>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-md bg-paper border border-hairline p-2">
              <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-ink mb-0.5">Low · 64%</p>
              <p class="text-xs text-ink leading-snug">Loaded language: "the so-called experts"</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Three-feature pitch -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-accent mb-6">What you get</h2>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-5">

        <div class="rounded-xl border border-hairline p-5">
          <p class="font-serif text-2xl text-accent mb-2">11</p>
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink-strong mb-2">Analytical lenses</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink leading-relaxed">
            The same engine that runs on the web. Toulmin decomposition, 26 named fallacies, loaded
            language, unstated warrants, key-term consistency, referential clarity,
            empirical testability, modal-scope check, and more.
            <a href="/how-it-works" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-support underline">Full breakdown →</a>
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-xl border border-hairline p-5">
          <p class="font-serif text-2xl text-accent mb-2">Toulmin</p>
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink-strong mb-2">Structural decomposition</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink leading-relaxed">
            Every audit returns the argument's claim, grounds, warrant, qualifier, and rebuttal -
            with the weakest link identified. The piece of scaffolding that, if removed, brings the
            argument down.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-xl border border-hairline p-5">
          <p class="font-serif text-2xl text-accent mb-2">∅</p>
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink-strong mb-2">Persistence-free reader mode</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink leading-relaxed">
            No account, no history, no server-side storage of what you're reading. The audit runs
            against the page and the result lives in the side panel for that session. Close the
            tab; it's gone.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Install -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-accent mb-4">Install</h2>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-paper p-6">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink-strong mb-2">Coming to the Chrome Web Store.</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink leading-relaxed">
          The extension is feature-complete and being readied for submission. For early access while
          it's in review, email
          <a href="mailto:daniel.livingstone44@gmail.com" class="font-semibold underline">daniel.livingstone44@gmail.com</a>
          and you'll get an unpacked build with install instructions.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA back to /reader -->
    <section class="mb-4">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-hairline p-6 flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-4">
        <div>
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink-strong mb-1">Prefer the web version?</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">
            Paste any text or URL at <span class="font-mono text-xs bg-hairline/40 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">/reader</span> - same engine, no install.
          </p>
        </div>
        <a href="/" class="shrink-0 inline-flex items-center justify-center px-5 py-2.5 rounded-md bg-accent text-white text-sm font-semibold hover:bg-accent/90 transition-colors">
          Open the Reader →
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
</Base>
